1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,335
2 PM

2
00:00:01,375 --> 00:00:03,665
Full sun on your rooftop solar…

3
00:00:03,705 --> 00:00:05,725
and suddenly, a power cut

4
00:00:06,278 --> 00:00:07,694
The sun is still shining

5
00:00:07,734 --> 00:00:08,954
But your fans stop

6
00:00:08,994 --> 00:00:10,903
Your solar isn't broken

7
00:00:10,943 --> 00:00:12,167
It switched off on purpose

8
00:00:12,207 --> 00:00:14,534
— to protect a lineman's life

9
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:17,090
Where does all that sunshine go?

10
00:00:17,130 --> 00:00:18,352
And how do you keep

11
00:00:18,392 --> 00:00:19,361
your fans running?

12
00:00:19,401 --> 00:00:20,000
Let's see

13
00:00:21,763 --> 00:00:22,663
One thing first

14
00:00:22,703 --> 00:00:24,196
— this is not the inverter

15
00:00:24,236 --> 00:00:25,948
battery you keep at home…

16
00:00:25,988 --> 00:00:27,445
It's the box your solar

17
00:00:27,485 --> 00:00:28,692
panels connect to

18
00:00:28,732 --> 00:00:30,313
Installers call it an

19
00:00:30,353 --> 00:00:31,663
on-grid inverter…

20
00:00:31,703 --> 00:00:33,787
We'll just call it the solar box

21
00:00:34,306 --> 00:00:36,075
Your panels give DC power

22
00:00:36,115 --> 00:00:37,594
— it flows only one way

23
00:00:38,119 --> 00:00:40,061
Your house runs on AC power

24
00:00:40,101 --> 00:00:41,590
— not the air conditioner,

25
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:42,682
the wall-socket kind

26
00:00:42,722 --> 00:00:44,352
It swings forward and back

27
00:00:44,392 --> 00:00:47,052
— 50 full swings every second

28
00:00:47,092 --> 00:00:48,556
The solar box turns panel

29
00:00:48,596 --> 00:00:50,490
power into wall-socket power

30
00:00:52,124 --> 00:00:52,812
Here's the thing

31
00:00:52,852 --> 00:00:54,719
— the solar box can't make that

32
00:00:54,759 --> 00:00:56,625
back-and-forth rhythm on its own

33
00:00:56,665 --> 00:00:58,672
Think of the grid as a drummer…

34
00:00:58,712 --> 00:01:00,835
and the solar box as a dancer

35
00:01:00,875 --> 00:01:02,517
that only follows the drum

36
00:01:02,968 --> 00:01:03,911
On a normal day,

37
00:01:03,951 --> 00:01:05,287
it follows every beat

38
00:01:05,327 --> 00:01:07,217
Your house uses what it needs

39
00:01:07,257 --> 00:01:08,563
The extra goes out

40
00:01:08,603 --> 00:01:09,639
through your meter…

41
00:01:09,679 --> 00:01:11,042
onto the street wire…

42
00:01:11,082 --> 00:01:11,780
and up to the

43
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:13,071
transformer on the pole

44
00:01:14,653 --> 00:01:16,218
Now the power cut comes

45
00:01:16,258 --> 00:01:17,887
The electricity board switches

46
00:01:17,927 --> 00:01:19,185
off the supply to your street

47
00:01:19,717 --> 00:01:20,401
Think about it

48
00:01:20,441 --> 00:01:22,455
If your solar box kept pushing,

49
00:01:22,495 --> 00:01:23,482
that dead wire would

50
00:01:23,522 --> 00:01:25,023
be alive again, right?

51
00:01:25,498 --> 00:01:26,723
And that transformer on

52
00:01:26,763 --> 00:01:28,199
the pole works in reverse

53
00:01:28,239 --> 00:01:30,298
Your 230 volts…

54
00:01:30,338 --> 00:01:32,727
becomes about 11,000 volts…

55
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:34,779
On a wire the lineman

56
00:01:34,819 --> 00:01:36,245
thinks is switched off

57
00:01:37,858 --> 00:01:39,129
So the solar box is

58
00:01:39,169 --> 00:01:40,221
built to notice

59
00:01:40,261 --> 00:01:41,786
If the beat goes missing,

60
00:01:41,826 --> 00:01:43,611
or the voltage starts changing,

61
00:01:43,651 --> 00:01:45,176
it switches itself off…

62
00:01:45,216 --> 00:01:45,614
click

63
00:01:45,654 --> 00:01:47,609
Safety rules say it must

64
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:49,355
switch off within 2 seconds

65
00:01:50,811 --> 00:01:52,693
But there's one tricky case

66
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:54,194
Say your whole street is using

67
00:01:54,234 --> 00:01:55,266
exactly what the

68
00:01:55,306 --> 00:01:56,553
solar panels make

69
00:01:56,593 --> 00:01:59,013
Then the power cut changes nothing

70
00:01:59,053 --> 00:02:00,351
— the box can't feel it

71
00:02:00,813 --> 00:02:02,674
So the box tests the drummer

72
00:02:02,714 --> 00:02:03,842
Again and again,

73
00:02:03,882 --> 00:02:05,244
it plays a little off-beat

74
00:02:05,284 --> 00:02:06,644
— on purpose — to check…

75
00:02:06,684 --> 00:02:08,851
is the drummer still there?

76
00:02:09,927 --> 00:02:11,186
If the grid is there,

77
00:02:11,226 --> 00:02:13,525
the drummer pulls it back in line

78
00:02:14,499 --> 00:02:15,498
If the grid is gone,

79
00:02:15,538 --> 00:02:16,746
nobody pulls it back

80
00:02:16,786 --> 00:02:18,660
The beat keeps sliding…

81
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:20,395
and the box knows. Click

82
00:02:20,435 --> 00:02:21,392
— it switches off

83
00:02:23,075 --> 00:02:24,462
What happens to your panels?

84
00:02:24,502 --> 00:02:25,703
Once the box is off,

85
00:02:25,743 --> 00:02:27,691
the power has nowhere to go

86
00:02:27,731 --> 00:02:28,689
Nothing comes out

87
00:02:29,186 --> 00:02:30,339
The sunlight still lands

88
00:02:30,379 --> 00:02:31,772
and just turns into heat

89
00:02:31,811 --> 00:02:33,998
— your panels are built for that

90
00:02:34,038 --> 00:02:35,674
But the panel wires still

91
00:02:35,714 --> 00:02:36,871
have voltage in them

92
00:02:36,911 --> 00:02:38,216
So don't touch them yourself

93
00:02:38,256 --> 00:02:39,929
— leave that to a trained person

94
00:02:41,443 --> 00:02:42,369
So how do you keep

95
00:02:42,409 --> 00:02:43,141
your fans running?

96
00:02:43,181 --> 00:02:44,982
You need a different box

97
00:02:45,022 --> 00:02:46,349
— a hybrid inverter

98
00:02:46,389 --> 00:02:48,253
Hybrid simply means it works with

99
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:50,156
the grid and with a battery

100
00:02:50,558 --> 00:02:51,535
When the grid dies,

101
00:02:51,575 --> 00:02:52,806
a switch inside it

102
00:02:52,846 --> 00:02:53,823
first cuts your house

103
00:02:53,863 --> 00:02:54,840
off from the street

104
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,044
Then the battery

105
00:02:56,084 --> 00:02:57,488
becomes the drummer,

106
00:02:57,528 --> 00:02:59,172
and the panels dance again

107
00:02:59,793 --> 00:03:00,620
Remember this

108
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:02,637
A normal on-grid solar box,

109
00:03:02,677 --> 00:03:03,898
with no battery,

110
00:03:03,938 --> 00:03:05,158
has to go silent

111
00:03:05,198 --> 00:03:06,167
when the grid goes

112
00:03:06,207 --> 00:03:07,243
That's by design

113
00:03:08,501 --> 00:03:09,676
If anyone offers to

114
00:03:09,716 --> 00:03:10,890
switch off this safety

115
00:03:10,930 --> 00:03:12,440
— just say no…

116
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:14,335
Because the lineman fixing your

117
00:03:14,375 --> 00:03:15,387
street is the one

118
00:03:15,427 --> 00:03:16,229
who gets the shock

119
00:03:17,346 --> 00:03:18,803
Your solar never failed

120
00:03:18,843 --> 00:03:20,230
It just lost its drummer

121
00:03:20,799 --> 00:03:22,214
But when the grid is live,

122
00:03:22,254 --> 00:03:23,185
how does that box

123
00:03:23,225 --> 00:03:24,883
turn sunlight into steady

124
00:03:24,923 --> 00:03:26,095
wall-socket power?

125
00:03:26,135 --> 00:03:27,435
Let's open it up next
